   "unmapped": [
    "odd-arm structure: all arms share natural parameter eta_2 except one odd arm with eta_1 != eta_2; goal is to identify the odd arm",
    "vector (multi-parameter) exponential family observations",
    "objective is total cost = stopping time + sum of switching costs g(a,a') with g_max < infinity",
    "per-hypothesis false detection constraints alpha_i"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "We consider the problem of detecting an odd arm from a set of $K$ arms of a multi-armed bandit under a fixed confidence setting, i.e., with a constraint on the probability of false detection. Each arm follows a distribution from the vector exponential family parameterised by the natural vector parameter $\\boldeta$. As the name suggests, all arms except the ``odd\" one have the same parameter. The actual parameters of the odd and non-odd arms are unknown... The decision maker also incurs a cost whenever he switches from one arm to another."
  }
